{
  "protocol": "# Unified prediction / recommendation improvement v2\n## Frozen user contract\n- 11 raw numerical inputs, stored training state, no training/RAW upload on inference.\n- Ni and Co separately learned. One shared candidate prediction table for all modes.\n- Joint mode: both requested floors; explicit distance-to-(100,100) or maximin choice.\n- Ni priority: maximize Ni, NO Co floor. Co priority: reverse. No acid/cost minimization.\n- Do not force modes to differ; retain range/support guards, report reasons separately.\n- Keep original raw, models and audit files immutable.\n## Predeclared comparison (before running experiments)\n- First 357 unique ordered RAW batches only; last 63 not scored or tuned.\n- Existing imputation and dictionary cleaning fixed, train-fold fit only.\n- Outer TimeSeriesSplit(3): 90/89,179/89,268/89; inner splits=3.\n- Primary baseline: frozen Ni ensemble / Co Ridge, REFIT on each outer training slice.\n- Auxiliary A11 Ridge for isolating features.\n- A17: raw 11 plus three process squares and three process pair products.\n- B17: A17 with logit(y/100) targets and 100*sigmoid inverse; eps=1e-5 only for exact endpoint labels.\n- Alpha grid .1,1,10,100 for all new Ridge candidates, selected by inner original-unit MAE.\n- A20/B20 diagnostic: add total impurity * (acid,temperature,time), no broad 38-feature search.\n- Selection evidence: MAE, RMSE, fold consistency, tail errors, train gap; not mode distinctness.\n- Do not trade away accuracy with an unannounced numerical tolerance. Promote bounded candidate only if both pooled MAE/RMSE improve versus frozen baseline and at least 2/3 fold MAE improve for that metal; require range check. Otherwise deliver explicitly marked trial candidate, not claimed final.\n- High-target small sample stats descriptive, not pass/fail or calibrated confidence.\n- Model and policy versions independent; policy single implementation for Colab + CLI.\n## Steps / tests\n1. RED/GREEN selector contracts: joint vs unconstrained priorities, conflicting and identical objectives, invalid outputs, filters, no-feasible and no-supported distinction.\n2. Reopen RAW and prior audits, refit candidates with fold-only stats; record every fold/candidate.\n3. Compare limited interactions, no automatic addition just for diversity.\n4. Stress same 151 complete materials x4140 candidates; per-axis response and selected points; dense-grid stability, fold-retrain stability diagnostic.\n5. Export selected numeric model / canonical no-fit runtime / standalone notebook built from same source; fresh process equality, immutable inputs, scalar-vs-batch consistency.\n6. Record limitations and evidence; no real-plant guarantee, no new independent holdout.\n",
